Two things worth your attention:

**The triage note under-corrected.** It recommended `'^### '`. That returns **4**, not 3 — `logs/incident-log.md:22` carries a literal `### YYYY-MM-DD — {short title}` inside the `## Schema` code block. I anchored on the ISO date instead (`'^### [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}'`), which is what line 3 of the script already specified. The note's failure-proof numbers also didn't reproduce — it claims the script printed `3` and that `grep -c '^### '` returns `1`; actual values were `2` and `4`. Its *mechanism* was right and I built on it; its counts are recorded as not reproducing rather than carried forward.

**Adjacent defect left alone, deliberately.** `logs/scripts/notify-check.sh:3-4` documents its own unfixed bug (`--level=warn` where `axcion-notify` expects `--severity=warn`) and consumes the same archival threshold. It's outside the Step 4 file set, so fixing it here would have been an opportunistic edit. It needs its own run.

Not committed — that's your call. If the fix looks right, commit per workspace rules; I won't push.
